---
// Privacy notice for the waitlist only. A starting template, not legal advice:
// review it (and replace it with a full policy) before the app itself launches.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { app } from '../app.config';

const updated = 'October 10, 2026';
---
<Base title="Privacy Policy" description={`How ${app.name} handles your waitlist signup.`}>
  <article class="wrap prose">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="meta">Waitlist notice. Last updated {updated}.</p>

    <p>
      {app.name} isn't released yet, so the only personal information we collect is what you give us when you
      join the waitlist. This page explains what that is and what we do with it. We'll publish a full privacy
      policy for the app before it launches.
    </p>

    <h2>What we collect</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Your email address.</strong></li>
      <li><strong>Optional answers</strong> about your position or role and your level, if you choose to give them.</li>
      <li><strong>Your consent</strong> and the time you gave it.</li>
      <li>
        <strong>Where you came from</strong>, such as "reddit" or "instagram", if the link you followed was labeled
        with one or your browser told us the site that sent you. See <a href="#source">How we know where you came
        from</a>.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>A scrambled version of your IP address</strong> (a one-way hash), used only to block spam and
        repeated signups. We never store your IP address itself.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Why we collect it</h2>
    <p>We use your email address to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Send you launch updates</strong> about {app.name}, including when it's out.</li>
      <li>
        <strong>Occasionally ask for your input</strong> to help shape {app.name}, for example a short survey, a
        request for feedback, or an invitation to try an early version. Answering is always optional.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We use the rest to see, in total, how much interest there is, from which positions and levels, and which
      places people find {app.name} through. We don't sell your information, share it for advertising, or add you
      to any other mailing list.
    </p>
    <p>
      To stop getting emails, reply to any of them and ask, or write to the address under
      <a href="#delete">Deleting your signup</a>.
    </p>

    <h2 id="source">How we know where you came from</h2>
    <p>
      Links we share can carry a label, such as <code>?utm_source=reddit</code>. When you arrive, the site keeps
      that label, or else the name of the site that sent you, in your browser's session storage. That storage
      belongs to the tab and is cleared when you close it. If you join the waitlist, the label is sent along with
      your signup. We use no cookies for this, and nothing is sent anywhere unless you sign up.
    </p>

    <h2>Who handles it</h2>
    <p>
      The waitlist runs on Cloudflare, which hosts the site and stores the signups for us. The form uses
      Cloudflare Turnstile to check that you're a person, not a bot. See
      <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" rel="noopener">Cloudflare's privacy policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
    <p>
      We keep your signup until six months after {app.name} launches, then delete it. You can ask us to delete
      it sooner at any time.
    </p>

    <h2 id="delete">Deleting your signup</h2>
    <p>
      Email <a href={`mailto:${app.privacyEmail}?subject=${encodeURIComponent(`Delete my ${app.name} waitlist signup`)}`}>{app.privacyEmail}</a>
      from the address you signed up with and ask us to delete it. We'll remove it and confirm within 30 days.
      You can also ask what we hold about you, or ask us to correct it, the same way.
    </p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>The waitlist isn't meant for children under 13. If you're under 13, please don't sign up.</p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>If we change this notice, we'll update the date at the top of this page.</p>
  </article>
</Base>
